{"name":"Beignet","hex":"#eccc9b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beignet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fritter (with a fruit or vegetable filling).","A Louisiana-style fried doughnut or fritter covered in powdered sugar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beignet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beignet","blocks":[{"text":"Beignet is a deep-fried pastry of French origin. It is commonly made from choux pastry, but can also be made using rice flour or yeast-leavened batters. Beignets can be served in a variety of preparations, the most common being dusted with confectioner’s sugar. The pastry is popular in French, Hungarian, Italian, Cajun, and American cuisines."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Beignet_good_for_mouth.jpg/330px-Beignet_good_for_mouth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beignet"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Beignets_de_pommes_de_terre.jpg/500px-Beignets_de_pommes_de_terre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Beignets_de_pommes_de_terre.jpg/1280px-Beignets_de_pommes_de_terre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Beignets_de_pommes_de_terre.jpg/500px-Beignets_de_pommes_de_terre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Beignets from Haute-Savoie","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeignets_de_pommes_de_terre.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Making_beignets_1.jpg/500px-Making_beignets_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Making_beignets_1.jpg/1280px-Making_beign